   "he": "נָפְלָה לְגִינָּה וְנֶהֱנֵית – מְשַׁלֶּמֶת מַה שֶּׁנֶּהֱנֵית. אָמַר רַב: בְּנֶחְבְּטָה;",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: If the animal «fell into a garden and derives benefit,» the owner «pays» for «the benefit that» it «derives. Rav says:» This is referring to a case «where» the vegetables softened the impact of «striking» the ground, and the owner pays for this benefit of the animal being saved from injury."
